@startuml
title M-SH2 - Controller recovery and controlled restart (SH2+ target)
actor "Initiating caller / optional board\ncaller account" as Caller
participant "swarma-session-host\nservice account / replacement controller" as Host
database "Host-private metadata, fences, epochs\ntranscripts, receipts, inbox, goal revisions\nowner: host" as State
participant "swarma-dispatcher\nexecution / capacity record owner" as Dispatcher
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot-owned generation ledger / exec.stop" as Manager
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nuser-manager module; root until UID/GID change" as Launcher
participant "swarma-session-runner\nworker-<label>; transport + lease owner" as Runner
participant "Harness / private Codex app-server\nworker-<label>" as Harness
participant "swarma-credential-broker\nCodex auth-owner refresh" as Broker

note over Host,Broker
  Target only: joint host_start / host_stop / session-scoped permit / runner-channel activation.
  Wire / proof formats and durable crash ordering remain unpublished (§3.3, §7).
  Dispatcher Unix-socket service (F-5/F-15): controls may serve with admission closed.
  Dispatcher slice 0 refuses interactive/resume; user-manager signed grants are v2.
  Current / SH1: tb-sessiond owns PTY/app-server; Claude dies on replacement.
end note

== Controller failure while execution may still live ==
Host -> State : reconcile durable fence / controller epoch before effects
note over Host,Runner : Nothing writes to runner before reconciliation (§3.4).
Host -> Dispatcher : recover: distinguish controller, runner, execution and unknown evidence
alt Live authenticated runner confirmed
  Runner <-> Host : re-authenticate / reconnect to replacement controller
  Host -> State : verified controller-only re-adoption under current epoch
  note over Host,Runner
    Keep execution ID; rotate execution-scoped authority on replacement.
    Account generation, execution ID and controller epoch are distinct.
    Reconnect channel and wire: unspecified in spec §7.
    FD3 carries only plan; no extra inherited descriptor assumed.
  end note
else Execution confirmed absent
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : absence permits capacity release / replacement; cleanup still requires recorded export or operator waiver
else Unknown or unreadable execution evidence
  Host -> State : keep fence closed / evidence unknown
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : keep capacity owned; no replacement or cleanup
end

== Separate scenario: authorised controlled restart (§3.5), only fence holder ==
note over Host,Runner
  Controller-only re-adoption above does not itself require an execution restart.
  Trusted standing sessions / executions have no preset lifetime or runtime limit.
  Only explicit stop, operator action (including emergency stop) or own exit ends a session.
  Park and controlled restart preserve the session; restart replaces only its execution.
  Dispatcher 12-hour maximum applies only to non-standing executions (§3.5).
  R-MAINT / dispatcher §11: close admission, inventory, operator-authorised exec.stop.
  Maintenance deadline bounds attempt, never session / execution lifetime.
  Require confirmed absence and reconciliation before mode/state/binary changes.
  Unknown/refused stop defers maintenance; keep standing allocations / identities.
  R-MAINT withdraws permit; restart needs fresh owner admission.
  No live supervisor adoption or automatic expiry.
end note
Caller -> Host : authorised restart / explicit recovery
Host -> State : hold delivery closed; invalidate pending interactions
Host -> Runner : drain external effects and child tools
note over Host,Runner
  Bounded note attempt may use marked snapshot fallback.
  Timeout never proves drain; explicit stop has no automatic restart.
  Drain protocol / failure disposition: unspecified in spec §3.5.
end note
Host -> Dispatcher : host_stop (dispatch-op/1); permitted execution / configured host principal
Dispatcher -> Manager : exec.stop (owned generation / execution)
Manager -> Manager : verify latest execution receipt / process identity
Manager -> Manager : TERM / grace / KILL all generation UID processes; stop user service domain
Manager -> Manager : verify account-wide absence over quiet period (F-13)
alt Process absence unresolved
  Manager -> Manager : absence unconfirmed; no successful stop return
  Host -> State : remain fenced; no replacement
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : retain capacity
else Process absence confirmed
  Manager --> Dispatcher : confirmed process absence only (exec.stop is harness-agnostic)
  Dispatcher --> Host : process absence confirmed
  Host -> Host : check binding, posture, authentication, grants, runtime
  alt Native resume requested with violated preconditions
    Host --> Caller : refuse incompatible version / family / home / profile / digest / auth / grants / transport
  else Supported recovery row and current authority
    note over Host,Harness
      Native resume: same machine, same major (0.x same minor),
      same runtime family / home / profile pin, intact transcript digest,
      exclusive native lock, ready auth and current grants; preserve transport.
      Unsupported recovery rows stay visibly parked or refused.
    end note
    Host -> State : prepare durable session intent / closed delivery fence; new execution ID
    Host -> Dispatcher : host_start (dispatch-op/1) with four per-start values / session-scoped permit
    Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : verify owner session lifecycle authorisation; same allocation / generation
    Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : prior claim absent; owner active; unchanged stored plan; fresh authority checks
    Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : idempotent logical_session_id / op_id; per-start claim / fence / receipt interlock
    alt Wrong principal / no lifecycle consent / retired owner / prior claim not absent / altered plan / cancelled claim / withdrawn or unresolved permit
      Dispatcher --> Host : refuse or reconcile; no new start
      Host -> State : keep delivery closed
    else Current per-start claim and session-scoped host admission permit
      Dispatcher -> Launcher : sole privileged start caller; existing claim / effect path
      Launcher -> Launcher : validate generation, executor, home and pinned exec-policy digest; refuse drift / all-stop mark; reset environment/descriptors\nexisting launch intent / atomic root start receipt
      Launcher -> Launcher : clear groups; set GID/UID
      Launcher -> Runner : exec approved runner; FD3 immutable plan only
      Runner -> Host : open fresh authenticated channel after UID change
      Runner -> Host : register admitted execution in current controller epoch
      Runner -> Runner : check harness native-lock absence under agent account / closed fence
      Runner --> Host : native-lock check result (report format unpublished)
      alt Native-lock result unknown
        Host -> State : keep session parked / delivery closed
        note over Host,Dispatcher : Unknown admission permits stay owned (§3.4).
      else Native lock confirmed present
        Host -> State : park; no harness initialisation / native resume / reopening
      else Native-lock absence confirmed
        Runner -> Broker : open broker connection after UID change (broker-mode Codex)
        Runner -> Runner : executor checks plan surfaces by digest or supplies root-owned surfaces outside home (R-STANDING)
        alt Surface drift
          Runner --> Host : refuse launch and report drift; code unpublished
          Host -> State : keep delivery closed; explicit re-materialization required
        else Surface verified / root-owned supply
          Runner -> Harness : initialise / native resume of admitted harness only under closed host fence
          alt Harness native resume fails
            Runner --> Host : resume-failed
            Host --> Caller : resume-failed; caller decides next action
            note over Host,Harness : No automatic fallback or portable seed on native resume.
          else Readiness unknown or re-authentication needed
            Runner --> Host : unknown readiness / authentication not ready
            Host -> State : park; keep delivery closed
          else Admitted readiness reported
            Runner --> Host : readiness after current-epoch registration / replayable start and readiness receipts
            Host -> State : reconcile dispatched input marker against intact transcript
            alt Matching marker
              Host -> State : receipt applied; no duplicate delivery
              Host -> State : reopen only after restart checks and reconciliation
            else Confirmed marker absence in intact transcript (ordinary input)
              Host -> State : redelivery permitted; reopen after reconciliation
              Host -> Runner : redeliver at turn boundary, same sender/message identity and op_id
              note over Host,Runner : This ordinary-input branch never auto-replays an unknown approval or control effect.
            else Unresolved evidence
              Host -> State : unknown; keep fence closed
              note over Host,Runner : Unknown approval answer / control effect never auto-replays.
            end
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
end

note over Host,Launcher
  Cancel before privileged call prevents call. After ambiguity, dispatcher resolves
  same effect ID and root receipt, stopping execution if required; never launch twice.
  Fence change withdraws affected start authority or requires reconciliation.
  Host failure retains dispatcher claim and closed fence until reconciliation.
  Wire / proof formats and acknowledgement-crash ordering: unpublished (§7).
end note
note over Host,Dispatcher
  R-SESSION: host_stop only by configured host principal for execution under permit.
  Journaled E-stop / exec.stop / confirmed absence; host-requested, distinct from owner cancel.
  host_stop confers no start authority.
  R-FATE: user manager §7 owns process-class fate table beside R-FD3.
  Survival and service-swap affected set require published unit / per-OS evidence.
  Dispatcher supervisor writes fenced by daemon-instance epoch; no live adoption.
  F-13: latest receipt authorises stop; signalling / absence scope is all UID processes.
  R-WATCH v0: journaled dispatcher exec.stop; affected-session hold / status-only observer reads.
  No v0 per-account egress freeze or phone alert; v1 freeze lifecycle remains open.
  Host parks or ends with durable reason; unknown absence keeps fence / claims.
  R-ALLSTOP: manual operator act closes every session delivery and snapshots bound boards.
  Dispatcher hold; range deny-all; stop every generation; freeze leases / renewals.
  Delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime; direct same-act fan-out / per-service journals.
  Prompt independent cuts; receiver launch/create/activation fence before absence scan.
  Operator-helper stops progress without dispatcher; every durable part required before recovery.
  Unknown keeps admission closed; recovery names stopped set / restart scope / owner authority.
  Keep fences until confirmed absence; explicit recovery only, no automatic restart.
  R-SVC-EGRESS: host deny-all, including loopback TCP; Unix-socket calls only.
  Readiness needs verified service row / anchor / resolver restriction (user manager §8).
  F-15: authenticated controls / observation / already-authorised stop stay reachable
  while forward admission is closed; unknown records retain claims.
  R-LOCK: no state lock across dispatcher or runner call; durable in-flight marker.
  Late results revalidated under lock; stale results never reopen delivery / admission.
  Detailed host wait/lock graph: M-SH5 / spec §3.4.
end note
note over Runner,Harness
  R-EXEC: machine-selected identity / body digest pinned at prepare; verify at start / retry.
  OS executable allowlist, writable areas non-executable; no self-started loops.
  Full invocation / transitive interpreted inputs qualified; no worker-selected code / plugins.
  Unprovable local tool routes to R-VERIFY; direct and indirect heavy forms refuse.
  R-STANDING: same check also before every initial launch; native resume never bypasses it.
  Host loop requires trusted class + local placement + admitted launch, never circle alone.
  Remote placement is workplace only even after circle admission; donor loop, no host session.
  Runner buffers bounded; dispatcher output-size invariant survives host handoff.
  Producer / aggregate retained debt survives replacement / retirement (§7.20).
  Protected control/evidence reserve supports stop / park / fence / reconciliation.
  Incomplete transcript never proves absence; remain closed / unknown.
  Enqueue / dedup / receipt lookup retain principal/id-to-complete-intent binding (§7.19).
  R-VERIFY: no builds / tests / worker-code execution in session account;
  separate-machine isolated ephemeral runners without secrets; board receives data.
  R-TRANSFER rework is new admitted base C plus findings in task snapshot,
  not the unchanged-plan successor path drawn here. Export precedes home deletion.
end note
